  <h1>Renting a car vs carpooling, and how to do both</h1>
  <div class="meta">Updated September 2026 · Prices are typical ranges; live seat prices are on each route page</div>

  <p class="lede"><strong>Short answer:</strong> a one-way rental from San Francisco to Los Angeles runs $80 to $200 for the day plus a one-way drop fee and a tank of gas, so $150 to $300 before you have driven anywhere. A Seat Sherpa carpool seat is capped at $55 plus a 5% fee. If you need a car at the other end, rent; if you only need to get there, take the seat. And if you rent anyway, you can post the trip on Seat Sherpa and let passengers cover a share of it.</p>

  <h2>Side by side, San Francisco to Los Angeles</h2>
  <div class="scroll"><table class="stack">
    <thead><tr><th></th><th>One-way rental</th><th>Seat Sherpa seat</th><th>Rent and post the ride</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Cost to you</td><td data-l="One-way rental">$150 to $300 (car, drop fee, gas, tolls)</td><td class="win" data-l="Seat Sherpa seat">$30 to $55 + 5% fee</td><td data-l="Rent and post the ride">Rental minus what passengers pay, often half or less</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Schedule</td><td class="win" data-l="One-way rental">Yours entirely</td><td data-l="Seat Sherpa seat">The driver’s posted time</td><td class="win" data-l="Rent and post the ride">Yours; passengers book around it</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Car at destination</td><td class="win" data-l="One-way rental">Yes</td><td data-l="Seat Sherpa seat">No</td><td class="win" data-l="Rent and post the ride">Yes</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Age and license rules</td><td data-l="One-way rental">Usually 21+, young-driver fee under 25</td><td class="win" data-l="Seat Sherpa seat">None to ride</td><td data-l="Rent and post the ride">Rental rules apply; Seat Sherpa verifies your license</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Insurance</td><td data-l="One-way rental">Rental counter coverage or your card’s</td><td data-l="Seat Sherpa seat">Driver’s policy; you are a passenger</td><td data-l="Rent and post the ride">Rental coverage; cost-sharing carpool passengers are permitted on most agreements, check yours</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table></div>

  <h2>Posting a ride in a rental</h2>
  <p>Seat Sherpa supports rentals. Post the route, date and seat price like any ride, and tell the app it is a rental; you add the make, model and plate the day before, once you have the keys. Passengers see the same verified profile and pay the same way, and seat prices stay under the cap. On a Friday SF to LA run with three passengers, the seats typically cover most of a one-way rental plus gas.</p>

  <div class="callout" style="text-align:center">
    <h3>See live seat prices on your route</h3>
    <p style="margin-bottom:6px">Drivers post trips they are already taking. Book in the browser or the app; no account needed to look.</p>
    <a class="btn" href="/rides?c=compare">Browse rides →</a>
    <p style="font-size:14px;color:#8a8a92;margin-top:10px">Driving somewhere yourself? <a href="/post">Post the ride</a> and split the cost.</p>
  </div>

  <h2>FAQ</h2>
  <div class="faq"><h3>Can I carpool in a rental car?</h3><p>Yes. Seat Sherpa lets drivers post a ride in a rental; you enter the vehicle details the day before the trip. Most rental agreements allow passengers on a cost-sharing basis, since no one is being paid for driving. Check your agreement and coverage.</p></div>
  <div class="faq"><h3>How much is a one-way car rental from San Francisco to Los Angeles?</h3><p>Typically $80 to $200 for the day plus a one-way drop fee that varies by company and season, plus gas. Budget $150 to $300 all in. A carpool seat on the same route is capped at $55 plus a 5% fee.</p></div>
  <div class="faq"><h3>How much does a Seat Sherpa seat cost?</h3><p>It depends on the route and the driver, but every seat has a hard cap: the IRS standard mileage rate (about $0.76 per mile in 2026) multiplied by the drivable miles, divided across the seats, and never more than $55 a seat. Riders pay the seat price plus a 5% service fee, shown before you pay. Live prices for each corridor are on the route pages and in the ride browser.</p></div>
  <div class="faq"><h3>Is Seat Sherpa safe?</h3><p>Every driver verifies a phone number by SMS, uploads a driver’s license that is checked for expiry, registers the vehicle, and connects a Stripe account that verifies identity and bank details. Riders see the driver’s photo, trip count and reviews before booking, can filter for women drivers, and can block anyone. A 4-digit pickup code confirms the rider got in the car and is what releases payment.</p></div>
  <div class="faq"><h3>What is the cancellation policy?</h3><p>One standard policy on every ride: cancel 24 or more hours before departure for a full seat refund, 2 to 24 hours before for 50%, and inside 2 hours there is no refund. The 5% service fee is non-refundable when the rider cancels. If the driver cancels, the rider gets 100% back including the fee.</p></div>

